   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch3/q4",
   "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\arccos\\left(\\frac12x\\right)\\qquad-2\\leqslant x\\leqslant2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has no stationary points. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The normal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, at the point where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\"></span>, crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span> is the origin,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>show that the area of the triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OAB\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{1}{54}\\left(p\\sqrt3+q\\pi+r\\sqrt3\\,\\pi^2\\right)\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> are integers to be determined. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
   "steps": [
