   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Explain why <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_1^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{x(2x+5)}\\,\\mathrm dx\"></span> is an improper integral. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li><p>Prove that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_1^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{x(2x+5)}\\,\\mathrm dx=a\\ln b\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are rational numbers to be determined.</p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
